+## C12 — Task-local Go build cache exhausts temporary disk
+
+- **Platform / signature:** Input-source workstream final scoped Go lint failed
+  typechecking with `write /tmp/memoh-input-source-gocache/...: no space left on
+  device`. The command exited 1; it was not an approval or access denial.
+- **Cause:** The task-specific Go build cache occupied 5.3 GB on the 8.8 GB
+  temporary filesystem after repeated compilation/lint work. No product or
+  database corruption was observed or inferred.
+- **Validated handling:** Confirm the failed lint has exited and no valid build
+  still uses that task cache; run `go clean -cache` with GOCACHE explicitly set
+  to that same disposable task directory. Preserve test logs, screenshots,
+  source, private configuration and all database/history records. Do not clean
+  shared or unidentified caches.
+- **Result / unresolved boundary:** Available space increased to 5.7 GB. The
+  original scoped lint was rerun with staged changes and exited 0, with no new
+  issues. This does not waive inherited lint findings, production validation,
+  or the independent C05 process-metadata denial.
+- **Original evidence:** Dedicated input-source workstream,
+  [disk-full result](session-input-source-20261030/go-lint-disk-full.log),
+  [final checks](session-input-source-20261030/checks.txt), and its README.
+- **New condition before another attempt:** Confirm the prior command exited,
+  the exact cache is disposable and task-owned, and adequate space was recovered.
+  Retry only the affected check; do not repeat unrelated paid calls or builds.
+
